# Caddyfile — HTTPS front door for the Portfoliarr stack.
# =======================================================
#
# WHY CADDY EXISTS HERE:
# Chrome will only install a site as a PWA from a SECURE CONTEXT — which
# means https:// or localhost. The home server serves plain HTTP on the
# LAN, so from the phone's point of view the app can never be installable
# (no prompt, and "Add to Home screen" creates a browser-tab shortcut).
# Caddy sits in front of the app and speaks HTTPS, which flips the origin
# into a secure context.
#
# WHY `tls internal` AND NOT LET'S ENCRYPT:
# A public certificate authority (Let's Encrypt etc.) can only issue
# certificates it can VERIFY — their challenges require the site to be
# reachable from the public internet. A home server on a LAN isn't, so a
# real cert is impossible without buying a domain + tunnel. Instead Caddy
# runs its OWN tiny certificate authority and issues a locally-signed cert
# for whatever site address is configured below. Browsers don't trust
# local CAs, so the phone shows ONE "Your connection is not private"
# warning on first visit — tap Advanced → Proceed anyway. After that the
# origin is a secure context and Chrome will offer the real install.
#
# THE SITE ADDRESS:
# {$PWA_SITE_ADDRESS} is read from the container's environment at startup
# (docker-compose.yml passes it through; the server's .env sets it to the
# server's LAN IP, e.g. https://192.168.1.50). Caddy then mints the
# internal certificate for exactly that host — including an IP SAN, which
# is what makes the phone's address bar warning the ONLY warning (no
# extra name-mismatch complaint). The :localhost fallback keeps the file
# valid on machines that never deploy. Give the server a static DHCP
# lease so its IP (and the cert's SAN) stay stable.
#
# Port note: Caddy listens on 443 inside its container; docker-compose.yml
# maps host 9968 -> container 443. The phone bookmark is therefore
# https://<server-ip>:9968.

{$PWA_SITE_ADDRESS:-https://localhost} {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy portfoliarr:5000
}